## Evidence shipped with the installer

- `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` identifies the open-source terms and source request procedure.
- `licenses/QT-6.12.0-THIRD-PARTY.html` includes all 138 component attribution pages linked from Qt's Qt 6.12.0 third-party inventory, with copyright and license texts.
- `licenses/QT-WEBENGINE-6.140.0-THIRD-PARTY.html` includes all 125 unique component license pages linked from the Qt WebEngine 6.140.0 inventory, including Chromium notices.
- `licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt`, `licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt`, root `LICENSE` (GPL-3.0-or-later), and `licenses/FDL-1.3.txt` provide the relevant full license texts.
- The build copies the exact bundled CPython, PyInstaller, and Inno Setup license files into the installer and records their versions in `licenses/BUILD_COMPONENTS.txt`.
- The build manifest records the bundled OpenSSL version; its Apache-2.0 license text is included as `licenses/OPENSSL-LICENSE.txt`.
- `SOURCE_OFFER.md` is shown before installation and promises complete corresponding Qt/PySide6/WebEngine source, build scripts, patches, and notices at no charge by electronic download for at least three years after the last distribution. GitHub Issues are the request channel.
- The offer identifies the official PySide6 6.12.0, Qt 6.12.0 module, and Qt WebEngine 6.140.0 source archives. The WebEngine source archive includes the corresponding Chromium source.

